# Extension metadata, read by the WebUI's extension catalog (configurator
# builds every card from the apt record). Omit a field and it silently falls
# back: no Extension-Name shows the raw package name, no Extension-Category
# files a player under "Tools". dpkg strips the XB- prefix in the built record.
XB-Hifiberry-Extension: yes
XB-Extension-Name: LMS (Squeezebox)
XB-Extension-Category: player
XB-Extension-Needs-Reboot: no
# Served by hifiberry-webui itself, so it resolves before the extension is
# installed and on a device with no internet access.
XB-Extension-Icon-Url: /images/svg/squeezelite.svg
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
         libflac14 | libflac12,
         libmad0,
         libvorbis0a,
         libmpg123-0 | libmpg123-0t64,
         libfaad2,
         hifiberry-configurator,
         adduser
Conflicts: squeezelite
Replaces: squeezelite
Provides: squeezelite
Description: Squeezelite - Lightweight Squeezebox player for HiFiBerry
 Squeezelite is a small headless squeezebox emulator for Linux designed
 to work with HiFiBerry audio hardware. It connects to Logitech Media Server
 to provide synchronized multi-room audio playback.
 .
 This package includes the Squeezelite binary optimized for HiFiBerry devices
 and configuration scripts for seamless integration with HiFiBerry OS.
